      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Andres :)\n\nSo, it\u0027s all about who is the one reading the log. An operator is the one going to be reading the log files, not a user or a keystone administrator. The operator is going to be looking at the log files when errors occur -- in order to identify the source of a failure.\n\nIn this case, there is no failure, nor is there any security risk. The action of returning a 403 is a normal part of the operation of Keystone, and therefore there should be no warning or error logged. Instead, the log message level should be info() -- since this log message is merely information and not meant to warn the operator that something is wrong -- or debug() -- a finer-grained level of information. I would argue that this information should be he debug() level of message.",
